---
title: Status and roadmap
summary: What is built and tested, what is deliberately out of scope so far, and the open gaps, ordered by the algorithms they block.
order: 5
---

## Built and tested

- Model building over typed quantities on flat and curved manifolds (SO(3), SE(3)), including
  discrete quantities.
- Evaluation of $\log p$, $\log q$ and the log-weight; first-order derivatives, Hessian–vector
  products, and the dense Hessian of $\log p$ (`hessian_hvp`); gradients of $\log q$ and $\log w$
  at given points (`log_proposal_ord1`, `log_weight_ord1`).
- Bindings, and the readers built on them: `residual_layout`, `residual_blocks`, `information*`,
  `GaussianBlock`, `coverage`.
- Block-sparse linearization: per-term Jacobians over only the quantities each term reaches, from
  one compressed reverse pass (`jacobian_blocks`), and `skoro-linearize` to turn a model into a
  Gaussian factor graph by its residuals or its Fisher roots.
- The Gaussian, with a Fisher root, and joint Gaussian factors.
- A compiler with an epoch-keyed cache, cut compilation, and slot liveness.
- Host `f64` dense factorizations, and GTSAM-style block elimination: COLAMD ordering, a reusable
  junction tree, multifrontal QR into a Bayes tree, and the solves on it (least squares, Fisher
  step, Laplace draws).
- Marginals by partial elimination — the Schur complement as a lower-triangular whitening — and
  the `JointNormal` built from one. A marginalizing window matches the full batch to rounding on a
  linear-Gaussian chain.

## Open gaps

| Gap | Blocks |
| --- | --- |
| No RNG seeding; no per-quantity sampling | Reproducible MCMC/SMC; per-chain streams |
| No reparameterization gradients (derivatives through samplers) | Reparameterized variational inference |
| Fisher assembly is not tape-differentiable | Riemannian-manifold HMC |
| No estimator, line search, or convergence test | Every deterministic estimator |
| Joint proposals over several quantities | Block proposals |
| Deferred bindings | Expensive-root families; very large models |

Details are in `docs/skoro.md` §5 and `docs/roadmap.md` in the repository.

